cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or the accompanying de-identified data, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "HB-TV-ExG: Hierarchical Bayesian Time-Varying Ex-Gaussian Modeling for Reaction-Time Vigilance Decrement"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation of HB-TV-ExG, a hierarchical Bayesian model in which the tail
  parameter of an Ex-Gaussian response-time density drifts linearly across a monitoring
  session. The model separates a static initial tail risk from an individual fatigue slope,
  yields a two-axis risk quadrant assignment, and is validated against a static-exposure
  variant with PSIS-LOO and WAIC, against competing response-time densities with a
  participant-cluster bootstrap, against four quality-control strategies, with a
  time-varying location ablation and subject-stratified 10-fold cross-validation, and with
  posterior quadrant classification probabilities, a posterior crossover-time distribution
  and posterior predictive checks.
